{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022732-interesting-character-concept-ideas","id":1022732,"title":"Interesting Character Concept Ideas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-27T07:09:14-08:00","id":1022732,"title":"Interesting Character Concept Ideas?","content":"What do you think would be an interesting character concept to play with and why? This can include any splat and subsplats or simple ideas for characters. <br /> <br /> One idea that fascinates me is the idea of a Ventrue Therapist who helps their patients by using Dominate to restructure the patient's mind into what they desire, or making mental problems become less pronounced. Kind of instilling the drive and letting the patient act it out themselves.<br /> <br /> The reason I think this could be interesting is because Dominate is more often than not to make people into servants, and the idea if there were no masquerade in the WoD that Mind Control powers would be heavily outlawed but I can see it having a potential market. Think about it, there's many people who have negative compulsions that harm their lives, be it a drinking problem, self-loathing that stems from abuse or the like. With those problems, I imagine powers that mess with one's mind would be seen as a potential solution. All of these reasons and finally the reason that a subversion to a vampire's predatory nature by helping people with their problems feels like a welcome idea to me.<br /> <br /> What are your ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T10:42:19-08:00","id":1022830,"title":"","content":"I had a similar idea. A Darkling who decided to dedicate their life to studying all the details of mortal and fae law. They would do this not only to protect their own Clarity, but also to be certain that their clients make informed decisions and don't suffer like they did for trusting blindly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T10:50:33-08:00","id":1022835,"title":"","content":"Person with family and 9-to-5 job. Some game lines, like werewolf, support this better than others, like vampire. First edition vampire put out the idea of Cleavers, vampires who tried to pretend everything was normal and life a normal life with their living family. Which I find incredibly interesting, though hard to pull off. Perhaps you could tell your spouse but convince the children you worked all day or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:04:35-08:00","id":1022982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022732-interesting-character-concept-ideas?p=1022835#post1022835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Person with family and 9-to-5 job. Some game lines, like werewolf, support this better than others, like vampire. First edition vampire put out the idea of Cleavers, vampires who tried to pretend everything was normal and life a normal life with their living family. Which I find incredibly interesting, though hard to pull off. Perhaps you could tell your spouse but convince the children you worked all day or something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How can you have a 9 to 5 if even the slightest bit of sunlight burns you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:16:25-08:00","id":1022988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022732-interesting-character-concept-ideas?p=1022982#post1022982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can you have a 9 to 5 if even the slightest bit of sunlight burns you?</div> </div> </div> </div>The 9-to-5 would fit more for others. Like I said, it doesn't work well with vampires. I suppose you could have some sort of work-at-home job, or a night job, as a vampire. 9PM to 5AM.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:55:52-08:00","id":1023009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022732-interesting-character-concept-ideas?p=1022835#post1022835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Person with family and 9-to-5 job.</div> </div> </div> </div>That fits Demons like a well tailored suit. They are <i>encouraged</i> to have the &quot;white picket fence&quot; package to further their disguise. Of course, they still have to explain an &quot;extra&quot; activities they might indulge in. So breaking out the Fight Club excuses may be needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022732-interesting-character-concept-ideas?p=1022988#post1022988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 9-to-5 would fit more for others. Like I said, it doesn't work well with vampires. I suppose you could have some sort of work-at-home job, or a night job, as a vampire. 9PM to 5AM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Developer job. No one expects us to see sunlight anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-27-2016, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T23:51:13-08:00","id":1023141,"title":"","content":"Priest turned vampire who strives to be 'good'. Joins the or do dracul to be able to learn to be more human. Funny enough this character manages to pull off the 9 to 5 as a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T08:58:48-08:00","id":1023297,"title":"","content":"A Beast Teacher that makes use of Atavisms like Siren's Treacherous Song, Eye of Heaven and Mimir's Wisdom to better teach children. Or a Daeva with high Presence holding seminars, or a Ventrue Tutor instilling a need for knowledge in his clients. For one, I would like to see a Character trying his best to improve other's lives in this manner, spreading Education and turning them into productive members of society, and two I think this route could go horribly awry, and then you'd have to deal with the mess =D Also, going to be a teacher, I know about some of the stress that job entails, and that made me wonder about how someone prone to Death Rage would deal with snotty brats and entitled princesses =D So Werewolf Teacher-on-the-run after a &quot;School Shooting&quot; would be interesting, too.<br /> <br /> A Werewolf Social Worker, trying to improve his client's lives through both mundane and supernatural means (Spirit of Poverty, begone! =P) Because I like it when, once in a while, human society and the pack's actions' consequences on it get focused.<br /> <br /> A character I'm actually playing online: A Gangrel &quot;from-rags-to-riches&quot; Professor, who managed to basically go Breaking Bad backwards: started as a dealer, got an interest in chemistry, got his life together, managed to get a stipendium, became a great chemist. Realized he liked to help people improve and become more than they are, and became a professor (the research was of secondary importance in that regard, though intriguing). Was actually embraced by &quot;accident&quot; (Oh shit, I killed him, shitshitshit, what do I do?! Oh wait, right, right, here, drink this! - along those lines). The prof managed to not die or kill due to sheer luck until he was taken in and educated about his new 'status'. Soon joined the Ordo. Is resentful about his Clan, since he feels it robs him of his intellectual edge (1ed, no 10-again on Intelligence-based rolls), but is exhilarated at the opportunity to improve himself once more. I like the idea of a character being deeply conflicted about part of what he has become, because it is in contrast to what he used to be or what is an integral part of his identity. Think Werewolf Pacifist or even Hippie, Nosferatu Model or Escort, Gangrel Monk, that type of thing.<br /> <br /> Promethean Movie-Star. Do I even need to explain? =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}